# SFA Development Standards (Strict)

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/18-DEVELOPMENT-STANDARDS.md` before any code change.

## MUST
- Modular: one domain = one NestJS module / React feature folder; logic in services & hooks
- DRY: search codebase first; shared DTOs in `packages/shared-types`; no copy-paste logic
- Minimal diff: only task-related files; no drive-by refactors, formatting, or dependency bumps
- Naming: DB `snake_case` + `comp_code`; API JSON `camelCase`; TS files `kebab-case`; use `compCode`, `dcr`, `rtp`, `pob`, `approveStatus` — no synonyms
- Tenant safety: every Prisma query scoped by JWT `compCode`; integration test for new data modules
- Atomicity: multi-step writes use `prisma.$transaction()` (submit+approval, POB lines, bulk upload)
- Tests: new endpoints need integration tests; new business rules need unit tests; bug fixes need regression tests
- i18n: English + Hindi + Hinglish via `packages/shared-i18n`; no hardcoded UI/API user strings; parity test for all keys
- UI design: loading/empty/error states; shared `components/ui/`; antd for new/touched tables/forms; see `sfa-ui-design.mdc`
- Library-first: use approved OSS libs (antd, TanStack Query, react-hook-form, dayjs, papaparse) — no reinventing wheels; see `sfa-library-first.mdc`
- Ports & adapters: services inject repository/storage/queue **ports** — Prisma/S3/Redis only inside adapters
- Microservice-ready: no cross-module DB access; use exported services or domain events + queue
- Observability: structured JSON logs with `requestId`, `compCode`, `module`, `action`; no console.log
- Config: `APP_ENV` dev/uat/prod via validated ConfigService — no hardcoded URLs/secrets in code
- Health: maintain `/health` and `/ready` (DB + Redis checks)

## MUST NOT
- Put business logic in controllers or presentational components
- Import another module's internal files or repositories (use module exports only)
- Unscoped DB queries without `compCode`
- Partial writes without transaction when failure causes inconsistent state
- Empty catch blocks; log errors, never log secrets
- Import PrismaService directly in business services (use repository port)

## Before finishing
Run lint + tests on affected packages. Confirm PR touches only related files.
